# Commit message template. Enable with:
#   git config commit.template .gitmessage
#
# Format: <type>(<scope>): <subject>       (max 72 chars, lowercase, no period)
# Types:  feat fix docs test refactor perf chore build ci
#
# Before committing: PYTHONPATH=src .venv/bin/python scripts/audit_defects.py
#
# The body is the traceability record. `git log --grep="Decision:"` should answer
# "why does this commit exist?" without reading the diff.

# --- What changed (bullets, imperative mood) ---


# --- Why it was needed (the problem, not the solution) ---


# --- Decision: alternatives considered and why rejected ---


# --- Evidence: tests, measurements, files proving it works ---


# --- Refs: backlog:<id>, phase:<n>, issue/PR links ---

